text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_scshle=§7- Added optional Biome Titles setting which prints a message when you enter a new Biome.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_kraihe=§7- Adjusted Custom Snow to not place Snow Layers by default.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_uhyntx=§7- Fixed Tumbleweeds not despawning in water.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ibbwxl=§7- Fixed the Sun Bloom being too bright in Snowy Biomes.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_rfghin=§7- Fixed an issue with Immersive (Extended) fog Render Mode not applying correctly.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_qgmscc=§7- Fixed an issue with the Nether fog not looking correct.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_pfrcad=§7- Ambiance sounds are now less affected by Server lag.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_qcxuvi=§7- Colour Grading Editor handles now uses drag control instead of click control.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_mzrdbz=§7- Removed developer assets that were left in the pack by mistake.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_cfvzsw=§7- Added a Firework Show, which will show up at Midnight!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_mnntvt=§7- Added customisable Sun and Moon textures, choose between Plain, Pixelated or HD, along with shape support for Square, Rounded Square, and Circle.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_rbexgp=§7- Fixed an issue causing Rain and Thunder to trigger too often.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_hztbqb=§7- Added new Always Winter toggle.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_mpvxvb=§7- Optimised Thunder Storm performance.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_adlugf=§7- General Performance Improvements in Multiplayer.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_aalggu=§7- Slightly increased Rain Drop ground Splash particle radius.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_odudjt=§7- Added a toggle to disable thunder when using Custom Thunder weather. You will still get Thunder visuals and sound, but there will be less fires.	#
ui.oreville_rb:lafxtwv.changelog_1_2.title=1.2 Update	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ejhort=§fHighlights	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_csqsfh=§fNew Content	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_elgrrx=§7- Added 3D items for all items in the pack, alongside improved hotbar textures for many existing items.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_kuqkxz=§7- Added Dynamic Lighting support for Copper Age game drop items, including the Copper Lantern and Copper Torch.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_pvgjjt=§7- Added custom Sulfur Caves fog and skybox visuals, surrounding the caves in a thick yellow haze.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ouhjwb=§7- Added surface level and underground audio ambiance for Sulfur Caves.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_zzaksp=§7- Added a Lens Flare Intensity slider, which defaults to 20 percent opacity.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ceyikf=§7- Added Light Ray Specks. Subtle floating pixels that look like they shimmer as they catch the light.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yfdule=§7- Added unique Light Ray colours to each biome. For example, they will be appear more green-tinted in the Jungle biome, and more purple-tinted in the Mushroom Island biome to better reflect the atmosphere.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_nwelzt=§7- Added Underwater Light Rays, which include underwater Light Ray Specks.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_paflhl=§7- Added a new 3D Sun & Moon setting, including support for moon phases.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_daqrcc=§7- Big behind-the-scenes rework for better performance, especially while playing with Vibrant Visuals enabled.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ygjzal=§7- Added a new Cloud Formation setting, allowing you to choose between Modern clouds and Legacy clouds.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_krcrbk=§7- §fModern §7clouds use the updated style introduced in the Chase the Skies game drop, with a cleaner and crisper look. This is the new default!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_qcdhey=§7- §fLegacy §7clouds use the original style from before Chase the Skies.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_jyfxij=§fImprovements	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_lmcgyx=§7- Reworked a large amount of the pack's core logic under the hood to improve performance. This should result in a smoother experience overall.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_evlmjq=§7- Disabled "Entity Light Sources" by default, and added a warning to highlight that it can be performance expensive.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_jcchea=§7- Players will now only receive the handbook the first time they join a world, preventing it from being repeatedly given out. It can still be crafted using 3 paper and 1 dirt.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_fvsgyj=§7- Removed the old permission system that required players to type a "§c/function§7" command.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yguyuu=§7- This has been replaced with an improved system based on your in-game permission level.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yapozf=§7- Players with "Operator" permission ("§c/op username§7") are now treated as trusted players and can manage settings requiring elevated permissions (such as applying settings to all players).	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yhbkkh=§7- New 3D items across the pack!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yutkyl=§fVibrant Visuals	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_gisjia=§7- Full support for Vibrant Visuals is unfortunately not possible just yet. In the meantime, we have made several smaller improvements to help Realistic Biomes work more comfortably alongside Vibrant Visuals. That said, Fancy Graphics remains our recommended way to play for the best overall Realistic Biomes experience. Once “Data Driven” graphics settings for Vibrant Visuals becomes available, we plan to include full support. We appreciate your patience.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_jinlfv=§7- Added coloured Dynamic Lighting when using Vibrant Visuals, allowing certain light sources to cast tinted light. For example, a Redstone Torch will now give off a red glow.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_yvakdg=§7- Added Vibrant Visuals support for glowing particles.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_vzpcsf=§7- Improved the appearance of bloom and lens flares in Vibrant Visuals.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_drtbwk=§7- Settings that are not currently supported by Vibrant Visuals are now disabled when using Vibrant Visuals. We hope to add support for these at a later date. This includes:	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_dskvwc=§8- Custom Skybox, Clouds, Sun and Moon.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_milgxx=§8- Colour Grading.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_glhssv=§8- Fog Rendering settings, which now default to Vibrant Visuals Fog Rendering.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_jqcjeq=§8- Ground Mist and Weather Mist. This change should significantly improve FPS while playing in Vibrant Visuals.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_xhyviw=§7- New Sulfur Caves atmosphere with ambience, fog and skybox visuals!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_atugcz=§7- Reduced the Aurora Borealis emission rate when using Vibrant Visuals, as large transparent particles can be very performance expensive. This change should significantly improve FPS while playing in Vibrant Visuals.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_dqqhar=§7- Added Vibrant Visuals compatible fog. §8Note: This does not currently look as good as we would like. At the moment, Vibrant Visuals Add-Ons do not allow us to adjust the skybox colour, and the skybox plays a large role in how fog colour appears. Because of this, the fog may look slightly grey or washed out for now.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_srnyry=§fFixes	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_wcroys=§7- Made significant performance improvements across the pack, especially to core systems that run frequently in the background.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_gbxtux=§7- Fixed an issue where weather would not trigger naturally in some worlds.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_ffzwxc=§7- Fixed an issue causing Marketplace skins and Persona items to render behind clouds instead of in front of them.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_qwzppq=§7- Tumbleweed will now instantly despawn when the setting is turned off.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_prfpvj=§7- Fixed Dripstone Cave underwater fog being so dense that visibility was almost completely blocked.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_irezfe=§7- Fixed an issue causing the world horizon to remain visible underwater. It should now appear as a clean blue view instead.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_xwagob=§7- Fixed an issue causing 50 percent of Light Rays to render invisible. Light Rays should now feel much more noticeable overall.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_zmfnsm=§7- New Light Ray Specks, and Underwater Light Rays for extra atmosphere!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_rrvtms=§7- Fixed an issue causing Wind Gust particles to display whilst underwater.	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_wkxrtc=§7- New 3D Sun & Moon setting with moon phase support!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_wvynrj=§7- New Cloud Formation setting with Modern and Legacy cloud styles!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_hkdcew=§7- Biome specific Light Ray colours!	#
text.oreville_rb.ui.oreville_rb:aelbwt_1_gorvjo=§7- Partial Vibrant Visuals support, including coloured Dynamic Lighting, lens flares, glowing particles and compatible fog!	#
